<title>MEXICO: Mexico awards Siemens $104 mln energy concession.</title>
<headline>Mexico awards Siemens $104 mln energy concession.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Federal Electricity Commission said on Wednesday it had awarded a concession worth $104 million to build three electricity substations to Germany's Siemens AG.</p>
<p>It said the substations were for the cities of Monterrey and Guadalajara.</p>
<p>It added the losing bidders were ABB Sistemas and AEG Energletchnik.</p>
<p>The electricity commission said it planned to grant a further 15 concessions between July and September worth $1.4 billion, including build-operate-and-transfer projects for several power plants such as Rosarito II, Monterrey II, Chihuahua and Cerro Prieto plants.</p>
</text>
